  "prefLabel": "Hedc 406.03 Accreditation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Hedc 406.03 Accreditation.\n\n(a) In lieu of conducting its own independent program or institutional evaluation, the commission shall accept accreditation by a regional or national agency recognized by the U.S. Department of Education, the Council for Higher Education Accreditation, or both, when the program or institution is in good standing with no special requirements.\n\n(b) For institutions not accredited by a regional or national accrediting agency recognized by the U.S. Department of Education, the Council for Higher Education Accreditation, or both, the commission shall conduct a comprehensive review every 3 years to determine continued program approvals.\n\n(c) An institution may make a written request to modify one or more of the requirements outlined in Hedc 405 for the purpose of initiating innovative modifications in academic programs or services. The request shall include the rationale and reason(s) for the modification(s) and require a majority vote of the commission for approval.\n\n(d) Any change in status with accreditor(s), including notices of concern or probation notification, shall be provided to the commission to determine compliance with Hedc 405.\n\nSource. #10429, eff 10-5-13 (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Hedc 400); ss by #13802, eff 11-2-23; ss by #14404, eff 10-15-25, EXPIRES: 10-15-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/hedc400.html"
